   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing. The image shows no stereo marks for the glutarimide carbon or the 1,4-disubstituted cyclohexane, so I left those unspecified. The spiro cyclohexane carbon is not a stereocentre, so it also has no stereo.\n\n**Fragments, from the bottom left of the drawing**\n- **Oxindole:** a 6-chloro-2-oxoindoline whose C3 is the spiro centre.\n- **Pyrrolidine:** the spiro carbon joins the pyrrolidine at C3. The ring then runs C4 (bearing a 3-chloro-2-fluorophenyl on a wedge), C5 (bearing the carboxamide on a hash), the ring NH, and C2, which is itself spiro to a cyclohexane.\n- **Linker, first part:** the C5 carboxamide is an anilide of a para-substituted benzene. That benzene carries a second amide, C(=O)NH, attached to a cyclohexane.\n- **Linker, second part:** the cyclohexane carries a CH2CH2 chain at its 4-position, and the chain ends on C4 of an isoindolinone.\n- **Cereblon ligand:** the isoindolinone nitrogen is bonded to a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl ring.\n\n**Stereocentres drawn with wedges or hashes**\n- Pyrrolidine C5 (hashed carboxamide) is `[C@@H]`.\n- Pyrrolidine C4 (wedged aryl) is `[C@H]`.\n- The oxindole spiro carbon (hashed aryl bond, wedged carbonyl bond) is `[C@@]`.\n\nI derived these tags by hand from the wedge and hash geometry, so the stereo assignment is the part I am least sure of.\n\nSMILES: O=C(Nc1ccc(cc1)C(=O)NC1CCC(CC1)CCc1cccc2c1CN(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)[C@@H]1NC2(CCCCC2)[C@@]2(C(=O)Nc3cc(Cl)ccc23)[C@H]1c1cccc(Cl)c1F"
